      "id": 1,
      "text": "Beulaville was founded in 1874 as a trading center for nearby farmers and logging and turpentine workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofbeulaville.com/community/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Beulah Baptist Church, which still stands as Beulaville Baptist Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beulaville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1916 residents funded the Duplin County Railroad, extending the Kinston line through Beulaville; the rail once ran beside present‑day Railroad Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beulaville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beulaville’s early school grew with three additions—an auditorium, gym, and band building—in 1923, and land purchases continued through 1950.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beulaville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town honors its heritage with local events and gatherings that celebrate community history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
